<article class="env-definition" id="0072">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0072">Definition <span data-tag="0072">6.9.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category with products. A presheaf $\mathcal{F}$ with values in $\mathcal{C}$ on $X$ is a <em>sheaf</em> if for every open covering the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{F}(U) \ar[r] &  \prod \nolimits _{i\in I} \mathcal{F}(U_ i) \ar@<1ex>[r] \ar@<-1ex>[r] &  \prod \nolimits _{(i_0, i_1) \in I \times I} \mathcal{F}(U_{i_0} \cap U_{i_1}) }  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equalizer diagram in the category $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article>